From 9decd54e34fd664480ac56f025d5f9ba24e43d92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 17:14:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add GPS module backed by the Android GNSS HAL over binder

LuneOS has had no GPS at all on Halium devices. com.webos.service.location is
built against the full nyx_gps_* API and ships in the image, but it opens
NYX_DEVICE_GPS and nothing on the hybris side provided one: nyx-modules' GPS
module drives a serial NMEA receiver and is enabled only for PinePhone and
PinePhone Pro, and nyx-modules-hybris had no GPS module.

Provide one. nyx's GPS API was modelled on the Android GPS HAL, so the
translation is close to mechanical - close enough that the numeric identity of
the mode, status, capability and location-flag constants is asserted at compile
time against <android/hardware/gnss-base.h> rather than assumed.

Binder rather than libhybris, because the legacy gps.h HAL reached through
hw_get_module() only exists pre-Treble; on the Halium bases we target, GNSS is
a HIDL service on /dev/hwbinder. That is the same reason led_controller.c
already falls back off the lights hw_module, and it puts this module alongside
the HIDL clients LuneOS already runs (ofono-binder-plugin, bluebinder,
sensorfw, nfcd-binder-plugin).

Which IGnss version a device exposes follows from the GSI flashed to it rather
than from the machine it was built from, so the instance is looked up at
runtime, newest first, and never chosen from cmake - the same reasoning that
governs the torch in nyx-modules/halium-arm64.cmake. We then speak @1.0 to
whichever instance answered: hwservicemanager registers a service under every
descriptor in its inheritance chain, and @1.1/@2.0 append methods rather than
renumbering inherited ones, so one code path covers every version.

Two conversions are not one-to-one and are done by hand:

- HIDL reports up to 64 satellites, nyx has room for 32.
- The legacy HAL and nyx describe ephemeris/almanac/used-in-fix as PRN-indexed
  uint32 masks; HIDL moved them to per-SV flags, so the masks are rebuilt from
  the flags. Only GPS satellites can be expressed that way without aliasing a
  non-GPS svid onto a GPS PRN, so other constellations are dropped from the
  nyx SV list rather than misreported.

Only the methods that are actually implemented are registered, so the A-GPS,
NI, XTRA and geofencing families answer NYX_ERROR_NOT_IMPLEMENTED. They need
the IAGnss/IGnssNi/IGnssXtra/IGnssGeofencing extension interfaces, which this
module does not fetch yet; registering them as successful no-ops would make
com.webos.service.location believe SUPL was configured when it was not.

Upstream-Status: Pending
